{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_3qmwsgpnnggznom57qowxru65f3pwfpumfej4dck77kaxo2o3svq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Rust implementation builds successfully and all tests pass. The translation is complete.\n\n**Summary of what was implemented in `src/ltre.rs`:**\n\n1. **`SymSet`** — 256-bit character set with empty/full/contains/insert/invert/union/intersect/is_empty operations, mirroring the C `symset_t` bitset.\n\n2. **`symset_fmt`** — Pretty-prints a `SymSet` into either positive `[...]` or complemented `^[...]` form, choosing the shorter representation. Handles special cases for `<>` (empty), single-symbol sets, and metacharacter/non-printable escaping.\n\n3. **`NState`/`Nfa`** — Index-based NFA representation (replacing C pointers with `Option<usize>` indices into `states` Vec). Includes `nfa_clone`, `nfa_concat`, `nfa_pad_initial`/`nfa_pad_final`, `nfa_uncomplement`, `nfa_dump`.\n\n4. **`DState`/`Dfa`** — DFA with 256-entry transition table, accepting/terminating flags, and powerset bitset. Implements LEB128/RLE serialization round-trip (`dfa_serialize`/`dfa_deserialize`).\n\n5. **Parsing** — Recursive-descent parser (`parse_regex` → `parse_term` → `parse_factor` → `parse_atom` → `parse_symset`) supporting alternation `|`, intersection `&`, complement `~`, `* + ? {n,m}` quantifiers, character classes `[...]`, intersection classes `<...>`, escapes (`\\n`, `\\xNN`, `\\d`, `\\s`, `\\w`, etc.), and `^` complement prefix.\n\n6. **`ltre_compile`** — Powerset construction followed by DFA minimization (table-filling algorithm with state merging and terminating-state flagging).\n\n7. **`ltre_matches`/`ltre_matches_lazy`** — DFA simulation, lazy compiles on first call.\n\n8. **`ltre_uncompile`** — Converts a DFA back to NFA via a binary-tree-of-epsilons construction, replicating the C source-state allocation strategy.\n\n9. **`ltre_decompile`** — State-elimination-based regex code generation with the same heuristics as the C version (in/out/self-arrow concatenation rules, \"nevermind\" fallbacks for symset boundary cases, alternation merging).\n\nAll 14 verification tests pass, covering basic matching, quantifiers, complement/intersection, partial/ignorecase, parse errors, serialization round-trip, decompile round-trip, lazy matching, fixed strings, and realistic regexes (HEX_RGB)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":158,"cache_read_input_tokens":99432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":158,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bacef50f-9625-45e4-b070-b3f990793217","uuid":"85462b92-5a4c-421a-bf1f-eaef14fe0f1d"}
